---
layout: base.njk
permalink: /404.html
eleventyExcludeFromCollections: true
title: "Page not found · baseline"
description: "That page is not here. Every documentation route is listed below."
---

<section class="section" aria-labelledby="nf-title">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="nf-head">
      <div class="hero-eyebrow">404</div>
      <h1 id="nf-title">That page is not here.</h1>
      <p class="doc-lead">The link may be old, or the page may have moved during the documentation rewrite. Every route is listed below, grouped the way the sidebar groups them.</p>
    </div>

    {# Built from docsnav.json, so a page that ships is reachable from here in the
       same edit that adds it. A recovery page that lists yesterday's routes is
       worse than no recovery page. #}
    {% for group in docsnav %}
    <h2 class="nf-group">{{ group.group or "Start here" }}</h2>
    {% if group.blurb %}<p class="nf-blurb">{{ group.blurb }}</p>{% endif %}
    <div class="grid-rule grid-3 lane-grid">
      {% for item in group.items %}{% if item.url %}
      <div class="cell">
        <div class="cell-kicker"><a class="link-inline" href="{{ item.url | rel }}">{{ item.label }}</a></div>
      </div>
      {% endif %}{% endfor %}
    </div>
    {% endfor %}

    <p>Still stuck? The <a class="link-inline" href="{{ '/' | rel }}">homepage</a> carries the install command, and issues go to <a class="link-inline" href="{{ site.repo }}/issues">the tracker</a>.</p>
  </div>
</section>
